```java
public static List<String> filterAndSort(List<String> list) {
    return list.stream()
            .parallel()
            .filter(s -> s.length() > 5 && !s.contains(" "))
            .sorted((s1, s2) -> s2.compareTo(s1))
            .collect(Collectors.toList());
}
```
In this implementation, we use the `parallel` method on the stream to enable parallel processing. This will help reduce the time complexity of the operation and improve performance for large input lists. Additionally, we use a single `sorted` operation instead of two separate operations, which will also help reduce the time complexity.

