2. Inorder Traversal of a Binary Search Tree
-----------------------------------------

An inorder traversal of a BST visits the nodes in the tree following a specific order: first, all the left child nodes are visited, then the root node is visited, and finally all the right child nodes are visited. To perform an inorder traversal of a BST in Java, you can use a recursive approach with a helper method:
