function gcd(x, y) {
  if (x < y) {
    return gcd(y, x);
  }
  if (x % y == 0) {
    return y;
  } else {
    return gcd(y, x % y);
  }
}
```
Explanation:
The above function uses the Euclidean algorithm to find the GCD of two numbers. It works by repeatedly dividing the smaller number by the larger number until the remainder is 0. The time complexity of this solution is O(log min(x, y)), which is the logarithm of the smaller of the two numbers.

