To validate the input fields, you can use JavaScript to check if the email address is in a valid format, if the age is a positive integer, and if the phone number is in a valid format with a country code. Here's an example of how you could implement this using JavaScript:
```
// Get all the form elements
const firstName = document.getElementById("first_name");
const lastName = document.getElementById("last_name");
const age = document.getElementById("age");
const email = document.getElementById("email");
const phoneNumber = document.getElementById("phone_number");
const message = document.getElementById("message");
const profilePicture = document.getElementById("profile_picture");

// Define a function to validate the input fields
function validateFields() {
  // Check if all the required fields are filled out
  if (firstName.value === "" || lastName.value === "" || age.value === "" || email.value === "" || phoneNumber.value === "") {
    return false;
  }

  // Check if the email address is in a valid format
  const re = /^(([^<>()[\]\\.,;:\s@"]+(\.[^<>()[\]\\.,;:\s@"]+)*)|(".+"))@((\[[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\])|(([a-zA-Z\-0-9]+\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}))$/;
  if (!re.test(email.value)) {
    return false;
  }

  // Check if the age is a positive integer
  if (age.value < 0 || !Number.isInteger(parseInt(age.value))) {
    return false;
  }

  // Check if the phone number is in a valid format with a country code
  const re = /^\+[1-9]\d{1,14}$/;
  if (!re.test(phoneNumber.value)) {
    return false;
  }

  // If all the fields are filled out correctly, return true
  return true;
}

// Add an event listener to the form submit button
const form = document.querySelector("form");
form.addEventListener("submit", (event) => {
  if (!validateFields()) {
    // Display error messages if any of the fields are not filled out correctly
    alert("Please fill out all required fields.");
    event.preventDefault();
  } else {
    // If all the fields are filled out correctly, submit the form
    return true;
  }
});
```
This code uses JavaScript to check if all the required input fields (first name, last name, age, email address, phone number) are filled out and if the email address is in a valid format, if the age is a positive integer, and if the phone number is in a valid format with a country code. If any of these conditions are not met, an error message is displayed and the form submission is prevented.

