To create a REST API with a resource named Transactions, you can follow these steps:

1. Choose a programming language and framework for your API. Some popular options include Node.js with Express.js or Python with Flask.
2. Define the endpoints for your API. For example, you might have an endpoint for retrieving all transactions (`GET /transactions`), an endpoint for creating a new transaction (`POST /transactions`), and an endpoint for updating a specific transaction (`PUT /transactions/{id}`).
3. Implement the logic for each endpoint using your chosen framework. For example, you might use SQL to retrieve all transactions from a database in the `GET /transactions` endpoint, or use a CRUD library to create a new transaction in the `POST /transactions` endpoint.
4. Test your API using tools like Postman or cURL to ensure that it is working correctly and responding with the expected data.
5. Deploy your API to a hosting platform such as Heroku or AWS to make it available for use by other applications.

Here's an example of how you might implement a simple REST API using Node.js and Express.js:
```
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const port = 3000;

// Define endpoints
app.get('/transactions', (req, res) => {
  // Retrieve all transactions from database
  const transactions = [...];
  res.json(transactions);
});

app.post('/transactions', (req, res) => {
  // Create a new transaction
  const { amount, description } = req.body;
  const transaction = { amount, description };
  // Insert transaction into database
  res.status(201).json(transaction);
});

app.put('/transactions/:id', (req, res) => {
  // Update a specific transaction
  const id = req.params.id;
  const { amount, description } = req.body;
  const updatedTransaction = { id, amount, description };
  // Update transaction in database
  res.json(updatedTransaction);
});

app.listen(port, () => {
  console.log(`REST API server listening on port ${port}`);
});
```
This is just a basic example, and you can customize the endpoints and implementation to meet your specific needs.

