    return max(dp[-1])
```
In this implementation, we use a two-dimensional array `dp` to store the results of subproblems. The first index of `dp` represents the position of the substring in the input string, and the second index represents the size of the substring. We initialize each element of `dp` to 0, and then fill it in with the appropriate values based on the recurrence relation.

The time complexity of this implementation is still O(n^2), but the space complexity is reduced from O(n^3) to O(n^2). This makes the function more efficient for larger inputs.

