Here is an algorithm to determine the most common element in an array:

1. Initialize a hash table to keep track of the count of each unique element in the array.
2. Loop through the array and for each element, increment its count in the hash table.
3. Find the element with the highest count by looping through the hash table and comparing the counts of each element.
4. Return the element with the highest count as the most common element.

Here is an example implementation in JavaScript:
```
function mostCommonElement(arr) {
  const count = {};

  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (!count[arr[i]]) {
      count[arr[i]] = 1;
    } else {
      count[arr[i]]++;
    }
  }

  let mostCommon = null;
  let highestCount = -Infinity;

  for (const element in count) {
    if (count[element] > highestCount) {
      highestCount = count[element];
      mostCommon = element;
    }
  }

  return mostCommon;
}
```
This algorithm has a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the array, because it only needs to loop through the array once to find the most common element. It also has a space complexity of O(1), because it only uses a hash table with a fixed size, regardless of the size of the input array.

