            for j in range(1, ni):
                for k in range(j + 1):
                    ways[j + 1] += ways[k - 1] * ways[j - k + 1]
            answer.append((ways[ni] % 109 + 7) % 109 + 7)
    return answer
```
This solution has a runtime of O(n\*k), where n is the length of the input array and k is the maximum value in the input array. The space complexity is O(k), as we need to store the counts for each subarray of length `ni`.

