  for (let i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (numSet.has(arr[i])) {
      return false;
    } else {
      numSet.add(arr[i]);
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```
This function uses a `Set` to keep track of the numbers that have been seen so far, and returns `true` if no repeating numbers are found, and `false` otherwise.

You can call this function on each of the arrays in turn, like this:
```
checkNoRepeatingNumbers(arr1); // returns true
checkNoRepeatingNumbers(arr2); // returns true
checkNoRepeatingNumbers(arr3); // returns true
...
```
This will tell you whether there are any repeating numbers in each of the arrays.

