To handle AWS credentials securely, you can use the following best practices:

1. Use environment variables or configuration files to store your AWS access key ID and secret access key, and avoid hardcoding them in your code. This will help prevent your credentials from being accidentally committed to version control systems or exposed in other ways.
2. Use secure storage mechanisms, such as AWS Secrets Manager, to store your AWS credentials and retrieve them at runtime. This will help ensure that your credentials are protected and only accessible to authorized users.
