```
function longestCommonPrefix(str1, str2) {
  const len1 = str1.length;
  const len2 = str2.length;
  let i = 0;
  while (i < len1 && i < len2 && !isNaN(parseInt(str1[i]))) {
    if (str1[i] !== str2[i]) {
      break;
    }
    i++;
  }
  return str1.substring(0, i);
}
```
This function uses a simple loop to iterate over both strings and checks whether the current character is a digit using `isNaN()`. If the character is not a digit, the loop breaks and the function returns the substring of the first string that is common with the second string up to the index `i - 1`.

