Please create a React component that allows users to add, edit, and delete items in a shopping cart.

The component should have the following requirements:

1. Accept a `cartItems` prop which is an array of objects representing items in the shopping cart. Each object should have properties such as `name`, `price`, and `quantity`.
2. Display the list of items in the shopping cart, including their names, prices, quantities, and total prices (calculated by multiplying the price and quantity).
3. Provide an interface for users to add new items to the shopping cart. This interface should include input fields for the item name, price, and quantity, as well as a button to add the item.
4. Allow users to edit the properties of existing items in the shopping cart. This should include changing the name, price, and quantity of an item.
5. Provide a way for users to delete items from the shopping cart.

Your implementation should have the following behavior:

1. Initially, display an empty shopping cart.
2. As the user adds items to the cart, display them in the list with their corresponding properties.
3. Allow the user to edit the properties of an item by clicking on it in the list and making changes in the input fields.
4. When the user clicks the "Add" button, add the new item to the list and recalculate the total price.
5. When the user clicks the "Delete" button next to an item, remove it from the list and recalculate the total price.
6. When the user edits the properties of an item, recalculate the total price accordingly.
7. Ensure that the interface is responsive and updates the list and total price in real time as the user makes changes.

You can use any additional libraries or frameworks as needed, but the core functionality should be implemented using React.

#Reference Code#
```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const ShoppingCart = () => {
  const [cartItems, setCartItems] = useState([]);
  const [newItemName, setNewItemName] = useState('');
  const [newItemPrice, setNewItemPrice] = useState('');
  const [newItemQuantity, setNewItemQuantity] = useState('');

  const addItem = () => {
    const newItem = {
      name: newItemName,
      price: newItemPrice,
      quantity: newItemQuantity,
    };
    setCartItems([...cartItems, newItem]);
    setNewItemName('');
    setNewItemPrice('');
    setNewItemQuantity('');
  };

  const deleteItem = (index) => {
    const updatedCartItems = [...cartItems];
    updatedCartItems.splice(index, 1);
    setCartItems(updatedCartItems);
  };

  const updateItem = (index, property, value) => {
    const updatedCartItems = [...cartItems];
    updatedCartItems[index][property] = value;
    setCartItems(updatedCartItems);
  };

  const calculateTotalPrice = () => {
    let totalPrice = 0;
    for (const item of cartItems) {
      totalPrice += item.price * item.quantity;
    }
    return totalPrice;
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>Shopping Cart</h1>
      <ul>
        {cartItems.map((item, index) => (
          <li key={index}>
            <input
              type="text"
              value={item.name}
              onChange={(e) => updateItem(index, 'name', e.target.value)}
            />
            <input
              type="number"
              value={item.price}
              onChange={(e) => updateItem(index, 'price', e.target.value)}
            />
            <input
              type="number"
              value={item.quantity}
              onChange={(e) => updateItem(index, 'quantity', e.target.value)}
            />
            <button onClick={() => deleteItem(index)}>Delete</button>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div>
        <input
          type="text"
          placeholder="Name"
          value={newItemName}
          onChange={(e) => setNewItemName(e.target.value)}
        />
        <input
          type="number"
          placeholder="Price"
          value={newItemPrice}
          onChange={(e) => setNewItemPrice(e.target.value)}
        />
        <input
          type="number"
          placeholder="Quantity"
          value={newItemQuantity}
          onChange={(e) => setNewItemQuantity(e.target.value)}
        />
        <button onClick={addItem}>Add</button>
      </div>
      <p>Total Price: {calculateTotalPrice()}</p>
    </div>
  );
};

export default ShoppingCart;
```

Note: The given code is correct and functioning as intended.

