```
def get_unique_elements(my_list):
    unique_elements = []
    for element in my_list:
        if element not in unique_elements:
            unique_elements.append(element)
    return unique_elements
```

This code uses a nested loop to iterate through the input list and checks each element against the elements already seen in `unique_elements`. If an element is not already in `unique_elements`, it is appended to the list. The time complexity of this approach is O(n^2) because the inner loop runs n times for each element in the input list, resulting in a total running time of O(n^2).

To achieve a better time complexity of O(n), we can use a dictionary to keep track of the unique elements. The dictionary will have the unique elements as keys and their counts as values. This approach has a time complexity of O(n) because the inner loop runs in constant time for each element in the input list, resulting in a total running time of O(n).
```
def get_unique_elements(my_list):
    unique_elements = {}
    for element in my_list:
        if element not in unique_elements:
            unique_elements[element] = 1
        else:
            unique_elements[element] += 1
    return list(unique_elements.keys())
