In this example, the `Object.create()` method is used to create a new object `lion` that inherits properties from an existing object `animal`. The `lion` object has two properties: `species` and `age`, which are inherited from `animal`. You can then add additional properties to the `lion` object using dot notation.

4. Using Object.assign(): You can also use the `Object.assign()` method to create a new object by assigning an existing object to it. For example:
