proc boxplot data=sashelp.cars;
  title "Box Plot of Horsepower";
  where origin="American";
  var horsepower;
  colorboxes / type=3;
run;
```
This will create a box plot with blue boxes and whiskers. You can also use different styles for the boxes and whiskers by using the `stype` option. For example:
```
proc boxplot data=sashelp.cars;
  title "Box Plot of Horsepower";
  where origin="American";
  var horsepower;
  colorboxes / type=1;
  stype=solid;
run;
```
This will create a box plot with solid, blue boxes and whiskers. You can also use other styles such as dashed or dotted by specifying the appropriate value for the `stype` option (e.g., `stype=dashed` or `stype=dotted`).

In addition to changing the color and style of the boxes and whiskers, you can also customize other aspects of the boxplot such as the labels, titles, and axis options. For example:
```
proc boxplot data=sashelp.cars;
  title "Box Plot of Horsepower";
  where origin="American";
  var horsepower;
  colorboxes / type=1;
  stype=solid;
  ylabel "Horsepower";
  xlabel "Origin";
run;
```
This will create a box plot with the same specifications as before, but with different labels and axis options. The `ylabel` statement is used to change the label of the y-axis from the default "horsepower" to "Horsepower". The `xlabel` statement is used to change the label of the x-axis from the default "origin" to "Origin".

