def get_pyramid(height):
    if height < 0:
        return []
    else:
        return [1] + get_pyramid(height - 1)
```
This code uses the same logic as before, but with an additional `if` statement to check if the input height is negative. If it is, the function returns an empty list instead of trying to access the element at index `-1` in the list. This ensures that the pyramid is inverted for negative heights.

