  if (target === array[mid]) {
    return mid;
  } else if (target < array[mid]) {
    return search(array.slice(0, mid), target);
  } else {
    return search(array.slice(mid + 1), target);
  }
}
```
This implementation uses a recursive approach to search for the target element in the array. The `search` function divides the input array into two halves and recursively calls itself on each half until it finds the target element or reaches the base case where the element is not found.

