function extractDomain(email) {
  // Split the email address into its parts
  const parts = email.split('@');

  // Get the top-level domain (TLD) and subdomain(s)
  const tld = parts[1].split('.').pop();
  const subdomains = parts[1].split('.').slice(0, -1).reverse();

  // Join the subdomains in reverse order to get the domain name
  let domain = subdomains.join('');

  // Add the TLD to the end of the domain name
  domain += '.' + tld;

  return domain;
}
```
This function uses the `split()` method to split the email address into its parts, and then uses `pop()` and `slice()` methods to extract the top-level domain (TLD) and subdomain(s), respectively. The `reverse()` method is used to reverse the order of the subdomains before joining them together to form the domain name. Finally, the TLD is added back to the end of the domain name using string concatenation.

