You are tasked with implementing a data structure to store key-value pairs and a function to retrieve the value associated with a given key. The data structure should support adding new key-value pairs, updating existing values, and retrieving values by their keys. Additionally, you need to write a function to perform a specific operation on the data structure and verify its correctness.

You are given the following code snippet as a starting point:

```rust
struct KeyValue {
    key: String,
    value: String,
}

struct DataStructure {
    values: Vec<KeyValue>,
}

impl DataStructure {
    fn new() -> DataStructure {
        DataStructure { values: Vec::new() }
    }

    fn add(&mut self, key: &str, value: &str) {
        self.values.push(KeyValue {
            key: key.to_string(),
            value: value.to_string(),
        });
    }

    fn update(&mut self, key: &str, value: &str) {
        for pair in &mut self.values {
            if pair.key == key {
                pair.value = value.to_string();
                return;
            }
        }
    }

    fn get(&self, key: &str) -> Option<&str> {
        for pair in &self.values {
            if pair.key == key {
                return Some(&pair.value);
            }
        }
        None
    }
}

fn main() {
    let mut target = DataStructure::new();
    target.add("1", "one");
    target.add("2", "two");
    target.update("2", "2");
    target.add("3", "three");

