This version uses a regular expression to extract the title and the name separately, based on the pattern `^([A-Z]\w*)\.\s*(.*)`. The `^` matches the start of the string, the `([A-Z]\w*)` matches any uppercase letter followed by any number of word characters, the `\.` matches a literal dot, and the `\s*` matches zero or more whitespace characters. The `(.*)` captures the rest of the string as the second group.

The `preg_match()` function returns `true` if the pattern is found in the string, and it returns an array containing all the captured groups. In this case, there are two captured groups: `$matches[1]` contains the title, and `$matches[2]` contains the name. If the pattern is not found, `preg_match()` returns `false`, and we print "No title found for name" instead.

