```
// This is a recursive implementation of the Fibonacci sequence
function fibonacci(n) {
  // Base case: If n is 0 or 1, return n
  if (n <= 1) {
    return n;
  }

  // Recursive case: Calculate the previous two numbers in the sequence and sum them together
  const previous = fibonacci(n - 1);
  const previous2 = fibonacci(n - 2);
  return previous + previous2;
}
```
This implementation has a time complexity of O(2^n), which is much faster than the original implementation for large inputs. Additionally, the comments explain the functionality of each line of code, making it easier for developers to understand how the function works and use it effectively in their code.

