        return False
    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):
        if n % i == 0:
            return False
    return True
```
In this implementation, we only need to check up to the square root of the number because any divisor greater than or equal to the square root is also a factor. By skipping over these larger divisors, we can significantly reduce the number of divisions required in the loop.

