    stack.push(1);
    stack.push(2);
    expect(stack.peek()).toBe(2);
  });

  it("should be able to clear the stack", () => {
    const stack = new Stack();
    stack.push(1);
    stack.push(2);
    stack.clear();
    expect(stack.size()).toBe(0);
  });
});
```
These test cases cover some basic operations on the stack, such as pushing and popping values, peeking at the top value, and clearing the stack. You can add more test cases to cover other functionality of the stack, such as iterating over its elements or checking if it is empty.

