class AdvancedQueue:
    def __init__(self):
        self.queue = []

    def enqueue(self, item):
        self.queue.append(item)

    def dequeue(self):
        if len(self.queue) == 0:
            return None
        else:
            return self.queue.pop(0)

    def size(self):
        return len(self.queue)

    def is_empty(self):
        return len(self.queue) == 0
```

```
// Optimized Bubble Sort Algorithm

// Define an array of numbers to be sorted
var arr = [1, 5, 3, 7, 9, 2, 4, 6, 8];

// Set a flag variable for tracking the status of the sort
var sorted = false;

while (!sorted) {
    // Initialize the swap flag to false
    var swapped = false;

    // Iterate over each element in the array
    for (var i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) {
        // If the current element is greater than the next element
        if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) {
            // Swap the two elements
            var tmp = arr[i];
            arr[i] = arr[i + 1];
            arr[i + 1] = tmp;

            // Set the swap flag to true
            swapped = true;
        }
    }

    // If no elements were swapped during the iteration, the array is sorted
    if (!swapped) {
        sorted = true;
    }
}
```
Here are some comments to explain the logic and steps of the optimized bubble sort algorithm:

1. `var arr = [1, 5, 3, 7, 9, 2, 4, 6, 8];`: This line defines an array of numbers to be sorted.
2. `var sorted = false;`: This variable is used to keep track of whether the array has been fully sorted or not. It starts with a value of `false`, indicating that the array is not yet sorted.
3. `while (!sorted) { ... }`: This loop iterates until the array is fully sorted. The loop runs as long as the `sorted` variable remains `false`.
4. `var swapped = false;`: This variable is used to keep track of whether any elements were swapped during the iteration or not. It starts with a value of `false`, indicating that no elements have been swapped yet.
5. `for (var i = 0; i < arr.length - 1; i++) { ... }`: This loop iterates over each element in the array, starting from the first element and ending at the second-to-last element.
6. `if (arr[i] > arr[i + 1]) { ... }`: This conditional statement checks if the current element is greater than the next element. If it is, then it means that the two elements need to be swapped.
7. `var tmp = arr[i];`: This line saves a copy of the current element in a temporary variable.
8. `arr[i] = arr[i + 1];`: This line replaces the current element with the next element.
9. `arr[i + 1] = tmp;`: This line replaces the next element with the saved copy of the current element.
10. `swapped = true;`: This line sets the `swapped` variable to `true`, indicating that at least one element was swapped during the iteration.
11. `if (!swapped) { ... }`: If no elements were swapped during the iteration, it means that the array is sorted and we can exit the loop by setting `sorted = true`.

By using this optimized bubble sort algorithm, we can save time by only iterating over the unsorted part of the array, which reduces the number of iterations required to sort the array.

