Here's an optimized version of the code that checks the length of the linked list and handles the case where it is empty:
```
public boolean hasCycle(Node head) {
    // Check if the linked list is empty
    if (head == null) {
        return false;
    }

    // Initialize two pointers, fast and slow, to the start of the linked list
    Node fast = head;
    Node slow = head;

    // Loop until the fast pointer reaches the end of the linked list
    while (fast.next != null) {
        // Advance the fast pointer by 2 nodes
        fast = fast.next.next;

        // Advance the slow pointer by 1 node
        slow = slow.next;

        // If the fast and slow pointers are equal, then there is a cycle in the linked list
        if (fast == slow) {
            return true;
        }
    }

