```
This code first checks whether the triangle is equilateral, then whether it is isosceles, and finally returns that the triangle is scalene if none of the above conditions are met. This makes the method more readable by breaking up the logic into separate branches. Additionally, PEP 8 recommends using `snake_case` for variable and function names instead of `camelCase`.

