```
function insertAtPosition(array, value, x, y) {
  const newArray = [];
  for (let i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
    if (i === x) {
      newArray[i] = [value];
      newArray[i + 1] = array[i];
    } else {
      newArray[i] = array[i];
    }
  }
  return newArray;
}
```
Explanation:

We iterate through the original multidimensional array and create a new array with the same length. When we reach the position `x`, we add an element to the array with value `value` at index `i`. We also add the elements from the original array starting from index `i + 1`. At the end, we return the new array.

Example:
```
const arr = [[0, 0], [1, 1]];
console.log(insertAtPosition(arr, 2, 1, 0)); // [[0, 0], [2, 1], [1, 1]]
```

