```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    char* haystack = "this is a test string";
    char* pattern = "*is*";
    int count = 0;

    // Use regular expression library to match wildcard pattern
    regex_t regex;
    regcomp(&regex, pattern, REG_EXTENDED);
    regexec(&regex, haystack, 0, NULL, 0);

    // If match is found, increment count
    if (regex.re_match) {
        count++;
    }

    printf("Found %d occurrences of pattern in haystack\n", count);

    return 0;
}
```
This code uses the `regex` library to match the wildcard pattern `*is*` in the string `haystack`. If a match is found, the count variable is incremented. At the end of the program, it prints out the number of occurrences of the pattern in the haystack.

