To check if two tree structures are identical at all levels and if they are mirrored images of each other, we can use a recursive approach. Here's an efficient algorithm:

1. Initialize two variables, `mirrored` and `identical`, to false.
2. Recursively traverse both trees simultaneously using two pointers. At each node, compare the data stored in both nodes. If they are not equal, return immediately with a value of false for `identical`. Also, if one tree is a mirror image of the other, then we can return false for `mirrored` immediately as well.
3. If both trees are identical and not mirrored images of each other, set `identical` to true.
4. If both trees are identical and also mirrored images of each other, set `mirrored` to true.
5. Return the value of `identical`.

Here's some sample Java code for this algorithm:
```java
public class Tree {
    int data;
    Tree left;
    Tree right;

    public static boolean areIdentical(Tree t1, Tree t2) {
        return areIdentical(t1, t2, false);
    }

    private static boolean areIdentical(Tree t1, Tree t2, boolean mirrored) {
        if (t1 == null && t2 == null) {
            return true;
        } else if (t1 != null && t2 == null || t1 == null && t2 != null) {
            return false;
        }

        // Check if the data stored in both nodes is equal
        if (t1.data != t2.data) {
            return false;
        }

        // Recursively check if the left and right subtrees are identical
        boolean leftIdentical = areIdentical(t1.left, t2.left);
        boolean rightIdentical = areIdentical(t1.right, t2.right);

        // If one tree is a mirror image of the other, then we can return false for mirrored immediately as well
        if (leftIdentical && !rightIdentical || !leftIdentical && rightIdentical) {
            return false;
        }

        // If both trees are identical and not mirrored images of each other, set identical to true
        if (leftIdentical && rightIdentical) {
            return true;
        }

        // If both trees are identical and also mirrored images of each other, set mirrored to true
        if (mirrored) {
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }
}
```
