2. Compare the data stored in both nodes using the `data` field of the node object. If they are not equal, return false for `identical`.
3. Recursively check if the left and right subtrees are identical using the `areIdentical` method. If one tree is a mirror image of the other, then we can return false for `mirrored` immediately as well.
4. If both trees are identical and not mirrored images of each other, set `identical` to true.
5. If both trees are identical and also mirrored images of each other, set `mirrored` to true.
6. Return the value of `identical`.

