If the number is negative, it adds a minus sign (-) at the beginning of the resulting string using the `operator+` overload for strings. Otherwise, it just converts the number to a string without any additional formatting.

Finally, if the number has scientific notation (i.e., the exponent is non-zero), it converts it to a string in scientific notation using `std::to_string` and adding the appropriate suffix ("e" followed by the exponent).

