The correct code to compute the sum of all prime numbers from 0 to n that are divisible by either 2, 3, or 5 is as follows:
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 100;
        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
            if ((i % 2 == 0 || i % 3 == 0 || i % 5 == 0) && isPrime(i)) {
                sum += i;
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Sum of prime numbers divisible by 2, 3, or 5 from 0 to " + n + ": " + sum);
    }

    public static boolean isPrime(int num) {
        if (num < 2) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 2; i <= Math.sqrt(num); i++) {
            if (num % i == 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```
