To implement the `basename` function for non-Windows systems, we can use the `std::string` class to manipulate the file path. Here's a possible implementation:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <string>

inline std::string basename(const std::string& filepath) {
    // Get the length of the file path
    size_t len = filepath.length();

    // Find the last occurrence of '/' in the file path
    size_t pos = filepath.find_last_of('/');

    // If there is no '/' in the file path, return the entire string
    if (pos == std::string::npos) {
        return filepath;
    }

    // Return the portion of the file path following the last '/'
    return filepath.substr(pos + 1);
}
```
