To correct this code, we can use a single thread to generate each element of the Fibonacci sequence using a recursive approach, as shown below:
```java
public class FibonacciThreads {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int max = Integer.parseInt(args[0]); // get the maximum value from the user input
        Thread thread1 = new Thread(() -> generateFibonacciSequence(max));
        thread1.start();
    }

    private static void generateFibonacciSequence(int max) {
