Here is a sample implementation of a JavaScript function that can extract the last k elements from an array and change their order from descending to ascending, without using built-in JavaScript Array methods:
```
function extractLastKElements(arr, k) {
  if (k > arr.length) {
    return [];
  }

  const extractedElements = arr.slice(-k); // extract the last k elements from the array
  extractedElements.reverse(); // reverse the order of the extracted elements
  return extractedElements;
}
```
This function first checks if the requested number of elements (k) exceeds the size of the array. If it does, it returns an empty array. Otherwise, it extracts the last k elements from the array using the slice() method and reverses their order using the reverse() method. The resulting array is returned.

