Here is an example of an algorithm that can multiply two numbers without using multiplication operator:
```
function multiply(a, b) {
  if (a < 0 || b < 0) {
    // If either number is negative, flip the sign of both numbers
    a = -a;
    b = -b;
  }

  let result = 0;
  while (a > 0 && b > 0) {
    if ((a & 1) === 1) {
      // If the least significant bit of a is set, add b to the result
      result += b;
    }

    // Shift both numbers by one bit to the right
    a >>= 1;
    b >>= 1;
  }

  return result;
}
```
The time complexity of this algorithm is O(log N), where N is the larger of the two numbers, because it only depends on the number of bits needed to represent the input numbers. The space complexity is O(1), because no additional memory apart from the variables needed for computation is used. This algorithm also handles negative numbers as inputs and returns the correct result.

