You are tasked with implementing a binary search tree (BST) in TypeScript. A binary search tree is a data structure that satisfies the binary search property: for each node `n`, all nodes in the left subtree of `n` have values less than `n`, and all nodes in the right subtree of `n` have values greater than `n`. Each node in the tree is represented by the following interface:

```typescript
interface INodeBase {
  value: number;
  left: INodeBase | null;
  right: INodeBase | null;
}
```

Your task is to implement a class `BinarySearchTree` that provides the following methods:
- `insert(value: number): void`: Inserts a new node with the given value into the BST.
- `search(value: number): boolean`: Returns true if the BST contains a node with the given value, otherwise false.
- `remove(value: number): void`: Removes the node with the given value from the BST, if it exists.

You should also implement a method `inOrderTraversal(): number[]` that returns an array of all node values in the BST using in-order traversal.

You should use the provided `INodeBase` interface for the node representation.

response:
Here is one possible implementation of the `BinarySearchTree` class in TypeScript:
```typescript
interface INodeBase {
  value: number;
  left: INodeBase | null;
  right: INodeBase | null;
}

class BinarySearchTree {
  private root: INodeBase | null = null;

  insert(value: number): void {
    const newNode = { value, left: null, right: null };
    if (this.root === null) {
      this.root = newNode;
    } else {
      let currentNode = this.root;
      while (currentNode !== null) {
        if (value < currentNode.value) {
          if (currentNode.left === null) {
            currentNode.left = newNode;
            break;
          }
          currentNode = currentNode.left;
        } else if (value > currentNode.value) {
          if (currentNode.right === null) {
            currentNode.right = newNode;
            break;
          }
          currentNode = currentNode.right;
        } else {
          // Value already exists in the tree, do nothing
          return;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  search(value: number): boolean {
    if (this.root === null) {
      return false;
    }
    let currentNode = this.root;
    while (currentNode !== null) {
      if (value < currentNode.value) {
        currentNode = currentNode.left;
      } else if (value > currentNode.value) {
        currentNode = currentNode.right;
      } else {
        return true;
      }
    }
    return false;
  }

  remove(value: number): void {
    if (this.root === null) {
      return;
    }
    let currentNode = this.root;
    while (currentNode !== null) {
      if (value < currentNode.value) {
        currentNode = currentNode.left;
      } else if (value > currentNode.value) {
        currentNode = currentNode.right;
      } else {
        // Value found, remove it from the tree
        if (currentNode.left === null && currentNode.right === null) {
          // Node has no children, simply remove it
          currentNode = null;
        } else if (currentNode.left !== null && currentNode.right === null) {
          // Node has only a left child, replace it with the left child
          currentNode = currentNode.left;
        } else if (currentNode.left === null && currentNode.right !== null) {
          // Node has only a right child, replace it with the right child
          currentNode = currentNode.right;
        } else {
          // Node has two children, find the minimum value in the right subtree and replace the current node with it
          let minRightNode = currentNode.right;
          while (minRightNode.left !== null) {
            minRightNode = minRightNode.left;
          }
          currentNode.value = minRightNode.value;
          currentNode.right = this._removeMin(currentNode.right);
        }
        break;
      }
    }
  }

  inOrderTraversal(): number[] {
    let result: number[] = [];
    this._inOrderTraversal(this.root, result);
    return result;
  }

  private _inOrderTraversal(node: INodeBase | null, result: number[]): void {
    if (node === null) {
      return;
    }
    this._inOrderTraversal(node.left, result);
    result.push(node.value);
    this._inOrderTraversal(node.right, result);
  }

  private _removeMin(node: INodeBase | null): INodeBase | null {
    if (node === null) {
      return null;
    } else if (node.left === null) {
      return node.right;
    }
    node.left = this._removeMin(node.left);
    return node;
  }
}
```
This implementation provides the required methods for inserting, searching, and removing nodes from a binary search tree. It also includes an `inOrderTraversal` method that returns all node values in the BST using in-order traversal. The `_inOrderTraversal` helper method is used to traverse the BST and collect the values of all nodes in the tree. The `_removeMin` helper method is used to remove a node with no left child (i.e., a "leaf") from the BST.

