This code is erroneous because it does not handle collisions properly. When multiple keys have the same hash value, the `put` method will overwrite the previous value stored for that key, and the `get` method will only retrieve the most recent value stored for that key. To fix this issue, we can use a linked list to store values for each key in case of collisions:
```
public class HashTable {
    private LinkedList[] table;

    public void put(int key, int value) {
        if (table[key] == null) {
            table[key] = new LinkedList();
        }
        table[key].addLast(value);
    }

    public int get(int key) {
        return table[key].getFirst();
    }
}
```
This code uses a linked list to store values for each key in case of collisions, allowing us to retrieve the most recent value stored for that key.

